# Acervator — .gitignore
# Principle: ignore only what is regenerable, transient, or oversized.
# Everything else is tracked.
#
# The cascade C00 "baseline snapshot protocol" section was removed under
# issue #67. It declared that `_archive/` and `.session26_backups/` were
# tracked on purpose, as a rollback mechanism. Measured 2026-08-22: neither
# directory is on disk and neither has a tracked file. The section named a
# protocol that protected nothing. Git history is the rollback mechanism.

# ── Python bytecode / build ─────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Build + distribution artefacts (71 MB, fully regenerable) ───
build/
dist/
*.manifest

# The version the build resolves and stamps into the bundle. It is written
# under build/ and reaches the bundle through the spec's datas, never the
# source tree; this line is the backstop if a copy is ever made here.
src/_baked_version.txt

# ── Tool caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.deepeval/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ── Runtime logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
_logs/
*.log

# ── Gate artefact ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by dev_harness/harness/check_release_readiness.py on every run.
# Tracking it would let a stale green sidecar ride into a commit.
.release_ready.json

# ── Oversized transient captures ────────────────────────────────
# 63 MB conversation-transcript backup; not source.
ACERVATOR_DEV_1_BACKUP_*.jsonl
pytest_out.txt
pytest_v3_*.txt

# ── Agent scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worktrees created for isolated agent runs. 1,414 files / ~30 MB were
# landing in the release zip before this rule; they are scratch, not
# project content.
.claude/worktrees/

# ── OS / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ── NEVER TRACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The operator's live runtime tree lives at ~/.acervator/ and
# ~/.acervator_logs/, outside this repo, and must stay outside it.
# These patterns are a backstop in case a copy is ever made here.
**/coinbase_credentials.json
**/bot_state.json
**/bot_state.backup.json
**/reservation_state.json
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# SADP deprecated 2026-08 - session backstop diffs, 71 MB, regenerable
.sadp/

# Written by tools/gate.py. Records WHICH COMMIT the gate proved, for the
# pre-push hook. Never commit it: it is per-clone and committing it would
# change the very sha it certifies.
.gate_stamp.json

# ── Per-clone harness state (regenerated at runtime) ────────────
# The touchset pin and island ledger both record an ABSOLUTE machine
# root (like .gate_stamp.json above). Committing them baked one Windows
# user's path into the repo; they are per-clone state, not source, and
# tools/touchset.py + tools/island.py rewrite them on the next run.
tools/.touchset_pin.json
tools/.island_ledger.jsonl

# Claude Code harness — hooks, skills and settings.
# Kept on disk, deliberately NOT tracked: the PreToolUse/PostToolUse archetype
# hooks fire on every Write|Edit and make interactive development unusable for
# a human developer, and settings.json carries bypassPermissions, which no one
# should inherit by cloning. Backup: acervator_claude_harness_backup_2026-08-25
.claude/*
# Shared guidance is not a hook and carries no permissions, so it is tracked.
!.claude/rules/

# Agent working files never enter the tree.
scratchpad/
